    <node id="孫詒讓">
      <data key="d0">孫詒讓</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">孫詒讓是清代學者，以《周禮正義》著稱，對《周禮》的研究做出貢獻。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be527ec0ce99fb40e90ea163df1654a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="賈公彥">
      <data key="d0">賈公彥</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">賈公彥是學者之一，其著作《周禮義疏》對《周禮》有解釋及分析。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be527ec0ce99fb40e90ea163df1654a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="河間獻王">
      <data key="d0">河間獻王</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">河間獻王是漢代的貴族之一，與《周禮》的流傳有關。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be527ec0ce99fb40e90ea163df1654a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="魯恭王">
      <data key="d0">魯恭王</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">魯恭王是漢代的貴族之一，與《周禮》的流傳有關。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be527ec0ce99fb40e90ea163df1654a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="孔安國">
      <data key="d0">孔安國</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">孔安國是漢代的學者之一，也與《周禮》的流傳有關。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be527ec0ce99fb40e90ea163df1654a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="孝經">
      <data key="d0">孝經</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">《孝經》 is a classic text in Confucianism that addresses the importance of filial piety and serves as a fundamental work influencing the moral principles in Chinese society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b09c1beeb6cdaac1d5c6fe2cd99821c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="曾子">
      <data key="d0">曾子</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Zengzi is a disciple of Confucius and is believed to have contributed to the teachings that led to the writing of《孝經》.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b09c1beeb6cdaac1d5c6fe2cd99821c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="戰國末年">
      <data key="d0">戰國末年</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The end of the Warring States period is a historical epoch in which《孝經》 is believed to have been composed, reflecting the philosophical developments of that time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b09c1beeb6cdaac1d5c6fe2cd99821c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="唐代">
      <data key="d0">唐代</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Tang Dynasty is notable for formally including《孝經》 in the canon of Confucian classics, further solidifying its importance in Chinese education and governance.&lt;SEP&gt;唐代是中國歷史上的一個重要時期，以其豐富的文化與學術交融著稱。&lt;SEP&gt;唐代是中國歷史上的一個重要時期，在學術和文化上具有統一和融合的特點。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b09c1beeb6cdaac1d5c6fe2cd99821c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f34dff0945453a5b68182bad891123d1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="《十三經注疏》">
      <data key="d0">《十三經注疏》</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">《十三經注疏》 is a collection of commentaries and explanations on Confucian classics, including《孝經》，compiled under the auspices of the Tang Dynasty.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b09c1beeb6cdaac1d5c6fe2cd99821c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="漢文帝">
      <data key="d0">漢文帝</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Emperor Wen of Han is known for promoting Confucianism and playing a role in the establishment of《孝經》 as an important text in the education system.&lt;SEP&gt;漢文帝 (Emperor Wen of Han) was instrumental in the elevation of 《爾雅》 to a classic status, establishing its authority in Chinese literature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b09c1beeb6cdaac1d5c6fe2cd99821c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76fef02a7da482530991d3fe525c8458</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="孟子">
      <data key="d0">孟子</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">《孟子》是記錄孟子及其弟子問答的經典，探討了氣、政治及仁義等主題。&lt;SEP&gt;孟子, known as Mencius, is a Chinese philosopher who elaborated on Confucian thinking and is considered one of the most significant figures in early Chinese philosophy.&lt;SEP&gt;孟子是孔子的繼承者，重視內在道德修養並提出了許多有關行天子之事的理念。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f88c28d67c43225bd395c7b72883c6d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5aaf763df3817bf1c61a76282875c415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ad40565e835fecb6dc58653b22f14d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="萬章">
      <data key="d0">萬章</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">萬章 is one of the disciples of Mencius involved in the compilation and editing of《孟子》 after Mencius's death.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aaf763df3817bf1c61a76282875c415</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="公孫丑">
      <data key="d0">公孫丑</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">公孫丑 is a disciple of Mencius who contributed to the collection and editing of the《孟子》 texts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aaf763df3817bf1c61a76282875c415</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="南宋朱熹">
      <data key="d0">南宋朱熹</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">南宋朱熹, Zhu Xi, was a prominent Confucian scholar during the Southern Song Dynasty who elevated the status of《孟子》 as part of the canonical texts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aaf763df3817bf1c61a76282875c415</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="《漢書・藝文志》">
      <data key="d0">《漢書・藝文志》</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">《漢書・藝文志》 is a historical record that documents the classification of Confucian texts, including《孟子》.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aaf763df3817bf1c61a76282875c415</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="《隋書・經籍志》">
      <data key="d0">《隋書・經籍志》</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">《隋書・經籍志》 refers to a literary record during the Sui Dynasty that catalogues classical texts, including《孟子》.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aaf763df3817bf1c61a76282875c415</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="北宋神宗">
      <data key="d0">北宋神宗</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">北宋神宗, Emperor Zhenzong of Song, was an emperor who promoted the study of Confucian texts, including《孟子》.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aaf763df3817bf1c61a76282875c415</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="滕文公">
      <data key="d0">滕文公</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">滕文公 is one of the figures mentioned in《孟子》, showcasing the political context and discussions relevant to Mencius's philosophy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5aaf763df3817bf1c61a76282875c415</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
