      <data key="d2">孫希旦 is a prominent scholar known for his analysis and commentary on classical Confucian texts, particularly his work《禮記集解》.&lt;SEP&gt;孫希旦 is a scholar known for his contributions to Confucian texts, particularly《禮記集解》.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b867defdd2d114136f6eb369213bd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="禮記集解">
      <data key="d0">禮記集解</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">《禮記集解》 is a compilation of commentaries by 孫希旦 on the Book of Rites, which elucidates rituals and moral conduct in Confucian philosophy.&lt;SEP&gt;《禮記集解》 is a compilation of commentaries on the Book of Rites, which is significant in the understanding of Confucian teachings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b867defdd2d114136f6eb369213bd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="郭店簡">
      <data key="d0">郭店簡</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">郭店簡 refers to a set of manuscripts discovered in Guodian, which provide insight into early Confucian thought.&lt;SEP&gt;郭店簡 refers to ancient bamboo slips discovered in Guodian that include early texts and commentaries related to Confucian thought, providing insight into early Chinese philosophy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b867defdd2d114136f6eb369213bd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="上博簡">
      <data key="d0">上博簡</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">上博簡 is a collection of manuscripts also relating to Confucianism, which helps to shed light on the development of Confucian ideas during the Warring States period.&lt;SEP&gt;上博簡 refers to a collection of bamboo texts that include works related to Confucianism, including themes explored in《禮記》.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b867defdd2d114136f6eb369213bd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="孔子閒居">
      <data key="d0">孔子閒居</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">孔子閒居 is a historical text depicting Confucius' reflections and teachings during his time away from public life.&lt;SEP&gt;孔子閒居 is a text that relates to Confucius' philosophies and teachings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b867defdd2d114136f6eb369213bd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="武王踐阼">
      <data key="d0">武王踐阼</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">《武王踐阼》 is a chapter in 《大戴禮》 that discusses the ascendancy of King Wu and its implications in Confucianism.&lt;SEP&gt;《武王踐阼》 is a section in《大戴禮》 that discusses King Wu's ascension and its implications for governance and morality in Confucian thought.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b867defdd2d114136f6eb369213bd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="曾子立孝">
      <data key="d0">曾子立孝</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">《曾子立孝》 is a chapter that delineates the importance of filial piety in Confucian ethics.&lt;SEP&gt;《曾子立孝》 is another section within《大戴禮》 that emphasizes the virtue of filial piety, which is central to Confucian ethics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b867defdd2d114136f6eb369213bd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="大戴禮記">
      <data key="d0">大戴禮記</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-635e67efc992a86fd06fbda104e7d526</data>
      <data key="d2">戴德's editing of《大戴禮記》 represents a significant effort to compile and disseminate critical writings on rituals.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="元明經學">
      <data key="d0">元明經學</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">元明經學 refers to the study of classical texts during the Yuan and Ming dynasties, characterized by the rigidification of scholarly practices due to the civil service examination system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d29ad594769c8b8c4a1737560d16e767</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="科舉制度">
      <data key="d0">科舉制度</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The 科舉制度 (Imperial Examination System) was a civil service examination system in China that played a central role in the selection of government officials during the Yuan and Ming dynasties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d29ad594769c8b8c4a1737560d16e767</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="朱子學">
      <data key="d0">朱子學</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">朱子學 (Zhuzi Learning) is the school of thought based on the teachings of Zhu Xi, which became the official academic doctrine during the Yuan dynasty.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d29ad594769c8b8c4a1737560d16e767</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="明代">
      <data key="d0">明代</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">明代 (Ming Dynasty) was a major historical period in China marked by significant cultural and scholarly developments, continuing the examination system inherited from the Yuan Dynasty.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d29ad594769c8b8c4a1737560d16e767</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="元代">
      <data key="d0">元代</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">元代 (Yuan Dynasty) was characterized by Mongol rule in China and a lack of focus on education, leading to the long-term neglect of the imperial examination system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d29ad594769c8b8c4a1737560d16e767</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="程朱理學">
      <data key="d0">程朱理學</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">程朱理學 (Cheng-Zhu School) is a branch of Zhuzi Learning focusing on the principles of the heart and nature, developed during the Ming Dynasty.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d29ad594769c8b8c4a1737560d16e767</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="反宋復漢">
      <data key="d0">反宋復漢</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">反宋復漢 refers to a movement during the Ming Dynasty aiming to restore Han cultural values and critique Song Dynasty philosophies, particularly opposing Zhu Xi's interpretations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d29ad594769c8b8c4a1737560d16e767</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="偽經之作">
      <data key="d0">偽經之作</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">偽經之作 (Pseudo-Canonical Works) refers to the phenomenon of forgery of classical texts that emerged during the Ming Dynasty, driven by scholarly superficiality and the pursuit of fame.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d29ad594769c8b8c4a1737560d16e767</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="呂柟">
      <data key="d0">呂柟</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">呂柟 is a notable scholar representing the Cheng-Zhu school, known for his work《四書疑問》 which discusses the Four Books and raises significant questions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d29ad594769c8b8c4a1737560d16e767</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
