      <data key="d0">王應麟</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">王應麟 was an influential figure in the study and collection of classical poetry during the Qing dynasty.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2052f122203d0c467d6ec2d975457a07</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="傅斯年">
      <data key="d0">傅斯年</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">傅斯年 was a noted scholar whose views contributed to the understanding of ancient language through works like the Book of Songs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2052f122203d0c467d6ec2d975457a07</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="古文學">
      <data key="d0">古文學</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">古文學 refers to the study and appreciation of classical Chinese literature, particularly poetry from earlier dynasties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2052f122203d0c467d6ec2d975457a07</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="班固">
      <data key="d0">班固</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ban Gu is a historical figure who suggested that 《論語》 was compiled by Confucius' disciples, contributing to the study of Chinese literature and history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8e859b9cfaecbe4f6dadf116534874f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="孔子弟子">
      <data key="d0">孔子弟子</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The disciples of Confucius, known collectively, are key figures in the transmission of Confucian teachings and participated in dialogues captured in 《論語》.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8e859b9cfaecbe4f6dadf116534874f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="姜子牙">
      <data key="d0">姜子牙</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Jiang Ziya is a legendary figure in Chinese history, though not directly related to 《論語》, is often discussed in the context of Chinese philosophical literature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8e859b9cfaecbe4f6dadf116534874f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="《四書章句集注》">
      <data key="d0">《四書章句集注》</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Collection of Commentaries on the Four Books is a significant work by Zhu Xi that includes interpretations of《論語》和 other Confucian texts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8e859b9cfaecbe4f6dadf116534874f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="吳承恩">
      <data key="d0">吳承恩</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Wu Cheng'en is a writer and historical figure mentioned in discussions about the significance of Confucian literature in the cultural sphere.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8e859b9cfaecbe4f6dadf116534874f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="秦漢時期">
      <data key="d0">秦漢時期</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Qin and Han Dynasties are significant periods in Chinese history when the early forms of Confucian thought were developed and standardized.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8e859b9cfaecbe4f6dadf116534874f</data>
